    "summary": "A woman&#039;s  outer headscarf, a &#039;kerpa ruva&#039;, or &#039;ruha&#039;.  Made of natural, cream-coloured cotton. Tabby woven bands with a thicker self colour weft evenly spaced throughout the centre field.  Towards each warp end are three bands of uncut laid-in work, set in a deeper cream field.  Two lines of black woollen thread laid in at each warp end.   Plied fringe with knot.",
